Sorry, I haven't posted the exact error because I thought it is quite speci=
fic to the recipe I'm building. My first question was also too vague, sorry=
 for that. The problem is that it fails in building that package because of=
 a missing file that should be populated by that dependency.

The error happens in the do_compile task:

>=20
> | make[1]: *** No rule to make target 'm4_image.bin', needed by
> 'flash_linux_m40'.=C2=A0 Stop.
> | make: *** [Makefile:23: flash_linux_m40] Error 2
> | WARNING: exit code 2 from a shell command.

So, the package expects that the file 'm4_image.bin' exists, and this file =
is generated by the dependency (it works well when building the yocto image=
, but not when building the SDK from scratch).

Thanks,
Alejandro

